## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region sagas with per-tenant isolation, durable storage, and reliable cleanup.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration across regions with CQRS and Event Sourcing
- Per-tenant event envelopes and outbox pattern
- Compensating actions and idempotent handlers
- Replay-safe projections and cross-region read-model updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch (pseudo)
function startSaga(tenantId, mediaId){
  const sagaId = uuid();
  persistSaga({id:sagaId, tenantId, mediaId, step:'Transcode', status:'in_progress'});
  publish({type:'Ingest', payload:{tenantId, mediaId, sagaId}});
}
function handleFailure(sagaId, failedStep){
  const comp = {Transcode:'DeleteTempArtifacts', PublishEU:'RevokePublishEU'}[failedStep];
  publish({type:'Compensate', payload:{sagaId, action:comp}});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency across services during retries?
- How would you observe and reconcile outbox vs. internal state across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design dynamic per-tenant policy enforcement in a Saga-driven architecture, including how to store, fetch, and react to runtime feature flags, and how to handle compensation when policy constraints change mid-flight. It also probes read-model migration strategies in an event-sourced, CQRS system.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy store with versioned flags
- Saga step gating and compensation
- Runtime policy changes and drift handling
- Read-model migrations with event-versioning
- Idempotency and outbox patterns

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator check before executing a step
function canRun(tenantId, sagaName, stepId) {
  const policy = policyStore.get(tenantId, sagaName, stepId);
  return policy?.enabled !== false;
}
```

```javascript
// React to policy changes: enqueue compensation if a gated step becomes invalid later
async function onPolicyChange(tenantId, sagaName, stepId, newPolicy) {
  if (!newPolicy.enabled) await compensationStore.enqueue({ tenantId, sagaName, stepId });
}
```

